{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4701",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa7 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participate in the same enzymatic activity. This activity is then directly associated with Ndufa7, indicating a potential mechanistic link between Metformin and Ndufa7. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, likely mediated by the inhibition of Nadh Dehydrogenase activity. The presence of multiple binding sites and the involvement of similar enzymatic functions support the idea that Metformin may modulate Ndufa7 through a common pathway, possibly by affecting the activity of the ubiquinone-dependent respiratory complex. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Ndufa7 in mitochondrial function and suggests that Metformin's effects on Ndufa7 may be relevant to its therapeutic action in metabolic disorders.",
